<title>UK: Shell Q4 current cost profits rise.</title>
<headline>Shell Q4 current cost profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to Dec 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p>Current cost net income excluding special items</p>
<p>				1,364		  vs 851</p>
<p> Final dividend Shell (pence) 22.5	   vs 20.4</p>
<p>Final dividend Royal Dutch (guilders)6.25 vs 5.60</p>
<p>FULL YEAR</p>
<p>Current cost net income excluding special items</p>
<p>				5,203		  vs 4,516</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had expected full year net income before exceptional items between 5.15 and 5.50 billion stg.</p>
<p>ROYAL DUTCH PETROLEUM</p>
<p> Fourth qtr shr (guilders) 5.04		vs 2.15</p>
<p> Year shr (guilders)     17.87		 vs 13.1</p>
<p>SHELL TRANSPORT</p>
<p> Fourth qtr shr (pence)  16.0		  vs 8.4</p>
<p> Year shr (pence)	  63.6		  vs 47.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Oil giant Royal Dutch/Shell Group is 60 percent owned by Royal Dutch Petroleum Co from the Netherlands, while Britain's Shell Transport and Trading Co Plc owns the remainder.  </p>
<p>FOURTH QUARTER GROUP RESULTS</p>
<p> Net proceeds		22,127		vs 18,329</p>
<p> Gross profit		4,875		 vs 3,451</p>
<p> Operating profit	  2,825		 vs 1,120</p>
<p> Interest income	   160		   vs 161</p>
<p> Interest expense	  170		   vs 189</p>
<p> Tax			   1,307		 vs 391</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN OF FOURTH QUARTER EARNINGS BY INDUSTRY SEGMENT.</p>
<p>Oil and gas exploration and production</p>
<p>				 1,010		 vs 491</p>
<p> Refining and Marketing  368		   vs 200</p>
<p> Chemicals		   139		   vs 17</p>
<p> Coal			  5.0 loss	    vs 13 profit</p>
<p> Other			 7.0 loss	    vs 4.0 profit</p>
<p> Minority interests	52 loss	     vs 5.0 profit</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
